<p>PHASE 6 =E2=80=94 MAKE ONE PROOFSPEC FULLY REAL</p>
<p>Start with a read-only claim because it has no authority complexity:</p>

<code>domain_available(domain)
</code>
<p>Flow:</p>
<ol>
<li>load domain_available.v1 ProofSpec.</li>
<li>make exact Claim.</li>
<li>registrar probe performs fresh provider check.</li>
<li>probe emits content-addressed Evidence.</li>
<li>QP resolves pinned judge.</li>
<li>judge returns TRUE/FALSE/UNKNOWN.</li>
<li>gates enforce freshness/provenance.</li>
<li>deterministic transition settles state.</li>
<li>QP signs TransitionReceipt.</li>
<li>store receipt/event.</li>
<li>replay from stored spec+claim+evidence+program manifest.</li>
<li>independent <code>receipt.verify</code> returns pass.</li>
</ol>
<p>Acceptance:</p>
<ul>
<li>changing one evidence byte -&gt; replay fail.</li>
<li>changing collector hash -&gt; fail.</li>
<li>stale evidence -&gt; fail/UNKNOWN according to protocol.</li>
<li>malformed registrar response -&gt; UNKNOWN.</li>
<li>NXDOMAIN alone cannot yield TRUE.</li>
<li>different domain cannot reuse evidence.</li>
<li>different ContractRoot cannot reuse receipt.</li>
</ul>
<p>PHASE 7 =E2=80=94 THEN BUILD THE FIRST REAL EFFECT: DOMAIN PURCHASE</p>
<p>Use these objects:</p>

<code>Claim A =3D domain_available(D)
